Z||000000||curtis||03-12-2001||01:46 PM||||<BR>Finally got my new suspension. Replaced everything, balljoints and poly all the way around. Went to get alighnment at Firestone $119 for a life time alighnment. When the went to pull out of the bay they broke my select cable for my shifter. Said they would pay for the part because I didn't want them working on it. So Ihad to drive home with first  and second gear. Well Ifixed that this weekend and finally got to drive more than 30 mph, It was scary the rear end sways back and forth. I thought Iwas going to lose it a few times so it has to go back to Firestone. Any ideas of what could be causing this. This sucks.||||reg||8
Z||000001||Bob Englert||03-12-2001||02:22 PM||||Did they give you a printout of the alignment specs?  If so, post the 'after' values and let see what they are set to.<P>I know from experience that it is very hard to get the slignment right when poly bushings have just been installed.  The car is so stiff that it doesn't settle quickly and it is very hard for the tech to get the values to be correct.  The tech needs to bounce the car a lot and wait awhile to let the car settle.<P>It is possible that if you had the car checked now it would not match the values on the printout when it left the shop.  <BR><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000002||Quadfiero||03-12-2001||02:24 PM||||Hey Curtis,<BR>Did they give you a print out on the alignment?  I replaced the struts on my 84 once and eye-balled the alignment. When I started to drive it to the alignment shop, the back end of the car would swing back and forth. I had a bad experience at an alignment shop and now I always ask for the print out. (not a good idea to get an alignment right before the shop closes. Sometime people want to go home more than they want to do a good job.) <BR>Hope you can get it straightened out. <BR>Bob<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||curtis||03-12-2001||02:35 PM||||I did get the print out but I don't have them here at work. I will post them as soon as I get home.||||reg||8
Z||000004||bHooper||03-12-2001||03:35 PM||||Curtis, I agree with everything that has been said (Bob, know's, he's done 3 cars and witnessed the results on mine).<P>I have poly everything, kyb's, eibachs, new ball joints, tie rod (both inner and outer), cam bolts, and rack.  The alignment shop did for squat on my car... no luck, gonna try someone else real soon. <P>On to the case at hand... have you looked at the tranny and engine mounts?  Do you have a rear swaybar?  Mine really wiggled in the rear, after alignment, and it wound up being the tranny and engine mounts!  They are available from advance auto, as well as wrenchead.com, so there is no need to pay the fiero store their outrageous prices.<P>good luck!<P><P>------------------<BR>hoop<BR>Red '86 GT<BR>KYB's, Eibach's,<BR>Poly Bushings||||reg||2
Z||000005||Larry Moss||03-12-2001||04:41 PM||||[Curtis:<P>Did you also replace the inner tie rods?  If the answer is yes, I would be inclined to think the motor / trans mounts are causing the problem.<P>I had a similar problem and solved it by replacing all of the above.  And, the results still were not that good.  (But I have not resulted to poly bushings or lowered springs).<P>Last, a really low profile tire, like Yoko's avs intermediates, really work well in the rear.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Jay||03-12-2001||04:47 PM||||All of the above and this.  Did you check the cradle bolts?  I know a guy that had loose cradle bolts that almost killed him, it's unlikely but just for saftey give those a torque down.  Especially if you've changed over to urethane cradle bushings, along with everything else.||||reg||1
Z||000007||curtis||03-12-2001||06:31 PM||||No rear sway bar. I did replace the inner tie rods and cradle bushings. The swaying is happening going straight down the high way. I did The supension weekend before last and drove an hour to get home and about an hour the following day and It had none of these systems. It actually drove better before. My front end also pulls hard to the left when I hit the brakes(scary). Anyways here are the actual number they gave me.<P>left front                    right front<BR>0.3              camber            0.4<BR>4.8              caster            3.8<BR>.16               toe              .16<BR>front<BR>cross camber  -0.1<BR>cross caster   1<BR>total toe      0.32<BR>set back       0.02<P>left rear                     right rear<BR>-0.9            camber          -0.8<BR>0.06             toe             0.17<P>rear<BR>total toe       0.23<BR>thrust angle   -0.06<P>the only thing that were out were right front toe, left rear camber and toe, right rear camber and toe, and rear total toe. This sucks I want to take some corners. I'm having withdrawls. <P>Thanks. <P><BR>||||reg||8
Z||000008||theogre||03-12-2001||08:02 PM||||the full alignment specs for 84-87(all) are in a thread here. try searching for caster and my user name at the same time. that should turn them up. (will save someone retypeing them.) Off top of my head those fronts don't sound very far off.<P>Acording to published GM specs I have rear toe should be Zero +-0.1 per wheel. (GM TSB 87-3-10 3/87 Rear Alignment Spec Change.) That would mean a total toe of .20 max I believe.<P>That thrust angle is pretty small. I can't remember that spec. have a good look at the front cradel bushings. Those getting crappy could cause thrust angle to change as you drive.||||reg||1
Z||000009||erapp||03-14-2001||01:34 AM||||IF i AM NOT MISSTAKEN YOU ALLWAY'S WANT MORE CASTER ON THE RT FRONT ABOUT .2 TO .5 TO KEEP IT FROM PULLING TO THE RIGHT AND YOUR TOE ADJUSTMENT ON THE REAR SHOULD BE THE SAME ON BOTH SIDE'S TO KEEP THE CAR FROM DOGLEGGING GOING DOWN THE ROAD. <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by curtis:<BR><B>No rear sway bar. I did replace the inner tie rods and cradle bushings. The swaying is happening going straight down the high way. I did The supension weekend before last and drove an hour to get home and about an hour the following day and It had none of these systems. It actually drove better before. My front end also pulls hard to the left when I hit the brakes(scary). Anyways here are the actual number they gave me.<P>left front                    right front<BR>0.3              camber            0.4<BR>4.8              caster            3.8<BR>.16               toe              .16<BR>front<BR>cross camber  -0.1<BR>cross caster   1<BR>total toe      0.32<BR>set back       0.02<P>left rear                     right rear<BR>-0.9            camber          -0.8<BR>0.06             toe             0.17<P>rear<BR>total toe       0.23<BR>thrust angle   -0.06<P>the only thing that were out were right front toe, left rear camber and toe, right rear camber and toe, and rear total toe. This sucks I want to take some corners. I'm having withdrawls. <P>Thanks. <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>||||reg||6
